  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe introduce a novel optimization strategy based on adaptive feature transformation and multi-timescale search. Unlike the previous stochastic methods, we apply a deterministic approach that adaptively transforms the optimization landscape to escape local optima. The core idea is to iteratively enhance the peaks of the function where high correlations occur, while maintaining integral constraints. This method focuses on both the structural properties of the optimal solution and the local behavior of the correlation function. We use a multi-resolution approach where we first optimize the global structure by focusing on the most significant peaks, then progressively zoom into finer details. This two-level optimization maintains the box constraints throughout the process by leveraging projection steps.\n\nMathematical specification:\n- Representation: Discrete probability vector h \u2208 [0,1]^N with \u2211h = N/2\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Formulation: We use a smooth, normalized version of the correlation function called the autocorrelation polygon (AP). The AP is defined as:\n  AP(h) = { \u2211_{i=0}^{N-1} h(i) [1-h((i+k)%N)] / (N/2) for k=0 to N-1 }\n- Transformation: We map the optimization variables h to new coordinates via:\n  v = log\u2082(h + \u03b5) - log\u2082(1-h + \u03b5)\n  where \u03b5 is a small constant for numerical stability.\n- Constraints: Enforced through projection onto the simplex:\n  proj(h) = clip(h, 0, 1) + (N/2 - \u2211clip(h,0,1)) / N \n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Initialization:\n   a. Start with provided `initial_h_values` (N=600)\n   b. Project to satisfy constraints: h \u2190 project_feasible(initial_h_values, N, N/2)\n   c. Compute initial correlation aperture\n\n2. Transformation step:\n   a. Transform variables: v = log\u2082(h + \u03b5) - log\u2082(1-h + \u03b5)\n   b. Minimize the maximum AP value in the transformed space\n\n3. Optimization loop:\n   a. Apply gradient-based optimization (L-BFGS-B) on v space\n   b. Use surrogate functions for AP\n   c. Project back: h \u2190 1/(1+exp(-v)) and clip(\u00b7, 0, 1)\n\n4. Adaptive enhancement:\n   a. Identify k with maximum correlation\n   b. Apply local transformation focusing on shifted regions\n   c. Refine using iterative proportional scaling\n\n5. Progressive resolution:\n   a. Coarsen selection window: reduce N by factor of 2 (then adjust integral)\n   b. Re-optimize at coarser scale (for faster evaluation)\n   c. Upscale to original resolution\n\n6. Hierarchical moves:\n   a. Level 0: Global rescaling\n   b. Level 1: Segment smoothing\n   c. Level 2: Peak enhancement\n   d. Level 3: Integral compensation\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n1. Transformation weight: \n   - Range: 0.5 - 1.5\n   - Initial: 1.0\n   - Adaptation: based on gradient information\n\n2. Pseudo-cost regularizer \u03b1:\n   - Base value: 1.0\n   - Update rule: \u03b1 \u2190 max(0.5 \u03b1, 0.95 \u03b1) on stagnation\n\n3. Multi-timescale selection:\n   - Timescales: [5, 10, 20, 40, N]\n   - Assign weights inversely proportional to timescale length\n\nComputebudget and robustness:\n- Primary estimation time: 60% of budget\n  - Initial search: 20% budget\n  - Progressive reduction: 30% budget\n- Monitoring checkpoints:\n  - At 10%, evaluate for stagnation\n  - At 40%, monitor gradient norms\n  - At 70%, compare against historical baseline\n- Projection frequency: every 10 gradient steps\n- Recovery strategy:\n  - If correlation estimate explodes, revert to last stable point\n  - Use grid interpolation for dimensional repair\n\nValidation and return contract:\n1. Feasibility checks:\n   - box constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n   - integral: |\u2211h - N/2| < 1e-5\n2. Objective calculation:\n   - Compute correlation polygon using FFT\n   - Verify against direct summation\n3. Termination conditions:\n   - Execution time \u2265 40% of budget OR\n   - No improvement in 30 iterations OR\n   - Objective under 0.3809 with statistical confidence\n4. Return triplet:\n   - h_values: final configuration (N=600)\n   - c5_bound: minimal correlated value\n   - n_points: 600 (fixed)\n\nFallback: If all solvers fail, return initial feasible solution with clipping.",
